  "findings": [
    "under the shipped 5.0s sqlite busy timeout the workflow load produced 0 `database is locked` errors; lock contention was absorbed as latency (claim/complete p95 7.102 ms over 6840 attempts), not surfaced as a conflict",
    "with the busy timeout cut to 0.02s the same load produced 256 lock conflicts and a retry amplification of 0.1123 retries per commit",
    "the workflow-layer conflict that does fire under the shipped configuration is the lease: 141 HELD_BY_LIVE_WORKER verdicts across 360 acquisitions",
    "the bounded budget (max_inflight=4, max_queue=4) refused 2880 admissions before any mutation; every scheduled activity still reached exactly one terminal receipt ({'COMPLETED': 360})",
    "concurrent writers to one project head saw a first-attempt success ratio of 0.3172 (437 RETRY_REQUIRED receipts over 640 first attempts); after bounded retry the eventual success ratio was 0.3172 with 0 untyped failures and 437 IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT on the retry the RETRY_REQUIRED receipt asked for; under a fresh-key-per-retry control the same load reached an eventual success ratio of 0.8750 (1659 key rotations, 560 commits)",
    "storage held 480 canonical records in 192512 bytes, 401.1 bytes per record",
    "the index-lag envelope is missed at cold start, not in steady state: pooled p95 43.0 events against a first-rebuild-per-repeat set of [120, 120, 120] and a steady-state p95 of 22.0 events",
    "the same workflow load repeated 3x produced per-repeat workflow-latency p95s of [1413.3, 1332.5, 2098.9] ms against a 2000.0 ms budget; the reported verdict is on the pooled 360-sample distribution"
  ],
